[orch:err] #### Issue body
[orch:err] issue: #49980
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## What changed
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] - Keep partial-update query and merge execution in Proxy.
[orch:err] - Resolve PChannel terms before allocating an attempt-scoped read timestamp.
[orch:err] - Carry encrypted term and read timestamp metadata with the insert payload.
[orch:err] - Add StreamingNode CAS admission using per-term PK versions and collection
[orch:err]   fences.
[orch:err] - Serialize CAS validation, WAL append, index publication, and transaction
[orch:err]   transition with the existing vchannel lock.
[orch:err] - Rebuild safe REPLACE attempts after deterministic CAS rejection.
[orch:err] - Preserve existing transaction recovery and replication behavior.
[orch:err] - Release partial-update proof state after a durable DropCollection.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Why
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] Concurrent partial updates can read the same row snapshot and subsequently
[orch:err] overwrite fields committed by another writer. The commit-side fence rejects a
[orch:err] mutation when the PK changed after the Proxy snapshot, preventing this lost
[orch:err] update without moving query or merge execution into StreamingNode.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Behavior boundaries
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] - AutoID partial updates are rejected.
[orch:err] - ARRAY_APPEND and ARRAY_REMOVE conflicts are non-retriable.
[orch:err] - Cross-vchannel atomicity and transaction-level exactly-once are unchanged.
[orch:err] - Concurrent Import, RestoreSnapshot, and backfill are outside this change.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Design
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] [Partial update optimistic lock design](docs/design-docs/design_docs/20260601-partial-update-optimistic-lock-design.md)
[orch:err] 
